so i've been recommending the magic  keyboard case for the ipad pro for  months now  since it literally takes your ipad to  the next level  and it actually makes it feel like a  macbook  and what does this is the fact that it  has a built-in  trackpad and this trackpad works  flawlessly  that's the main reason why i absolutely  do not recommend  the bridge pro plus keyboard case the  trackpad is  horrible and you're gonna end up being  disappointed  even though you saved money compared to  the magic keyboard  which works incredibly well and it's  about to get even better with ipad os 14  now that apple is allowing game  developers to add  keyboard and mouse gaming to the ipad  which is an absolute game changer so  your best choice was just to invest  300 dollars for the magic keyboard case  and have an  excellent overall experience however  there is one huge reason why you should  actually  wait and hold off on buying that magic  keyboard case  just yesterday logitech announced their  brand new folio touch keyboard case  with the trackpad for the ipad pro and  it's only  dollars so it's basically half off the  price of the magic keyboard  and it has two major benefits compared  to the magic keyboard which i'll get  into in just a moment  but first i want to mention two things  number one is that this keyboard totally  came as a surprise  and number two is that our premium apple  product hoodie is  incredibly soft and you can find it in  our merch shelf right below this video  about four months ago when the magic  keyboard case was just released  logitech also released trackpad keyboard  cases  for the ipad and the ipad air so it's  obvious that logitech was working  closely with apple to get it done  however they didn't release one for the  11 inch ipad pro  and now i finally know why if logitech  released this 160  keyboard case at the same time as  apple's magic keyboard  there would be a lot of people who would  have chosen this cheaper one instead so  what apple did was they made a deal with  logitech  where they wouldn't be able to sell  their folio touch for the ipad pro  until four months after the magic  keyboard case went up for sale  yes this does suck for the people who  would have preferred  to just buy the cheaper case instead but  in reality  the magic keyboard case is so good and  totally unique  that people who bought it are extremely  happy with it  almost every comment we received from  people who actually bought the magic  keyboard case  is very positive but right now  everything has  changed and honestly this logitech folio  touch  for 160 dollars is an absolutely  killer deal and i honestly think they  should have priced it at two hundred  dollars  because it's gonna kill the two hundred  dollar bridge pro  plus keyboard case the number one reason  why it's so good  is because it's the only third party  case for the new ipad pro  that can take advantage of the smart  connector  everyone else has to use bluetooth using  the smart connector means you have a  hardwired connection  from the ipad to the keyboard and the  trackpad  this means absolutely no lag no  reliability issues that come with  bluetooth  and no batteries that need to be  recharged  i know all of this because this new  folio touch keyboard case  is almost identical to the combo touch  that i already reviewed and compared to  the magic keyboard case  the only difference is the cutout at the  top for the apple pencil's wireless  charging  and the fact that the keyboard portion  isn't detachable  because the smart connector is on the  back of the ipad pro instead of on the  side  so based on my experience with the combo  touch for the budget ipad  this new folio touch for the ipad pro is  gonna work flawlessly  the trackpad experience was perfect and  the most important feature  is that it supports all of the same  gestures that you get with the magic  keyboard case  like swiping up with three fingers to go  to the home screen  swiping side to side with three fingers  to switch between apps  and perfectly smooth scrolling and  swiping  which you don't get with the bridge pro  plus keyboard case  so now i want to finally get into the  two major benefits  compared to the magic keyboard case  other than the obvious price difference  this folio touch actually has a top row  of function keys  which is probably the number one thing  that people complained about with the  magic keyboard  since it doesn't have that so now you  have an escape button to take you to the  home screen  you have brightness controls keyboard  backlighting controls  media controls like volume and more and  the other major feature is that you can  actually flip the keyboard portion  under the ipad pro so you can lay it  flat on a table  and more conveniently use your apple  pencil to draw or take notes  which isn't possible on the magic  keyboard case unless you take the ipad  pro  off and as a bonus this folio touch case  actually protects the sides of the ipad  pro which the magic keyboard  doesn't and it uses a very nice  fabric-like material  that won't get scuffed up over time like  the magic keyboard could  so all of that sounds great and honestly  for only 160 dollars  it's hard to justify spending the extra  cash on the magic keyboard  but there are also some downsides with  logitech's case  first of all there isn't a version for  the 12.9 inch model of the ipad pro  so if you have one of those the best  option is still  the magic keyboard case and another  downside of the folio touch is that it's  a lot thicker  than apple's case here's how the combo  touch version for the ipad compared  now it won't be this big of a difference  but it's definitely more thick  and finally there are three totally  unique features  that you get on the magic keyboard that  you can't get  on the new folio touch but instead of  just talking about those features i'm  gonna  show them to you when we receive it on  monday and compare it to the magic  keyboard  so if you're not already subscribed do  so right now  down below so you don't miss out because  that's gonna be a very  in-depth hands-on comparison and you'd  be surprised  you might actually want to spend the  extra 140  on the magic keyboard case based on  those three features  but if you're 100 dead set on buying  this folio touch  i'm going to leave some links down below  so you can order one before it goes out  of stock because i think these are gonna  fly off the shelves  but until monday if this video helped  you out go ahead and tap the like button  and click the circle above to subscribe  so you don't miss out on that comparison  video  and be sure to check out our apple  product merch right below this video  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one

